(1031533, 123286, 7364, '<td valign="top">not only the oldest authority, but quite possibly the oldest Bible too!  I like this photo.  Iw ould suggest cropping out the wood stand entirely though.  The orangy background is a real nice texture and color.  The wood is neither a good texture or color.  The white reflection is especially distracting.  Maybe if there was a cloth over it or something it would be more appealing, but my suggestion for a simple solution is to crop the left right up to the edge of the "H" and a little off the right for balance.  And finally, perhaps a WB adjustment or a warmer light on the bible cover, the contrast to the background is nice but it''s a bit too harsh.  Maybe it''s just the reflection from the spine.</td>', 'not only the oldest authority, but quite possibly the oldest Bible too!  I like this photo.  Iw ould suggest cropping out the wood stand entirely though.  The orangy background is a real nice texture and color.  The wood is neither a good texture or color.  The white reflection is especially distracting.  Maybe if there was a cloth over it or something it would be more appealing, but my suggestion for a simple solution is to crop the left right up to the edge of the "H" and a little off the right for balance.  And finally, perhaps a WB adjustment or a warmer light on the bible cover, the contrast to the background is nice but it''s a bit too harsh.  Maybe it''s just the reflection from the spine.', '2004-11-24 14:24:30.000000', NULL, 1),
