(1039701, 123505, 26401, '<td valign="top">I really do appreciate the comments!<br/> <br/>Although it may not be immediately apparent it was raining and that was the mood I was trying to capture... people having to wait for a light to change. I thought the lady with the umbrella would tell part of this story which is why she was left in. The guy on the other side of the street looks in a bad mood although that''s hard to see in the small print.<br/> <br/>There is not a lot of time to compose when the light doesn''t stay red for that long. I was also a bit concerned about getting the camera wet.<br/> <br/>I find that for the few challenges I''ve entered so far I don''t get an idea until the last day or two and then it''s a bit of a rush to put together and it rarely turns out to be something that I''m all that happy with, but I guess we all work under the same conditions.<br/> <br/>Perhaps next year when I''m retired my entries will get better.</td>', 'I really do appreciate the comments! Although it may not be immediately apparent it was raining and that was the mood I was trying to capture... people having to wait for a light to change. I thought the lady with the umbrella would tell part of this story which is why she was left in. The guy on the other side of the street looks in a bad mood although that''s hard to see in the small print. There is not a lot of time to compose when the light doesn''t stay red for that long. I was also a bit concerned about getting the camera wet. I find that for the few challenges I''ve entered so far I don''t get an idea until the last day or two and then it''s a bit of a rush to put together and it rarely turns out to be something that I''m all that happy with, but I guess we all work under the same conditions. Perhaps next year when I''m retired my entries will get better.', '2004-12-01 01:14:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1039729, 123483, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by graphicfunk:</b></div><hr/><i> Hey Paul; just want to know that this remains a very strong image. One of the few that impressed me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks.<br/> <br/>I had two purposes in positioning the shell in front. Mostly it was to obscure part of the type on the badge -- the the type was supposed to be readable, showing that part would have diluted the effect.<br/> <br/>Afterwards, I decided I also liked the was the round, crimped top of the shell mirrored the shape of the Seal.<br/> <br/>I had no intent to attribute this to the Bush (or any other particular) Administration -- that badge is the only one I happened to have around. If I could have gotten one which said <b> <br/>MI-5<br/>#007</b> <br/>believe me I would have used that instead!<br/> <br/>While "police" authorities do not (in the USA) have the right to go around shooting people indiscriminately, there''s ample evidence to show that they <b>do</b> shoot people <u>discriminately</u>, and are rarely punished for the resulting homicides, even when they involve the death of unarmed suspects or innocent bystanderd</td>', 'Originally posted by graphicfunk: Hey Paul; just want to know that this remains a very strong image. One of the few that impressed me.  Thanks. I had two purposes in positioning the shell in front. Mostly it was to obscure part of the type on the badge -- the the type was supposed to be readable, showing that part would have diluted the effect. Afterwards, I decided I also liked the was the round, crimped top of the shell mirrored the shape of the Seal. I had no intent to attribute this to the Bush (or any other particular) Administration -- that badge is the only one I happened to have around. If I could have gotten one which said  MI-5#007 believe me I would have used that instead! While "police" authorities do not (in the USA) have the right to go around shooting people indiscriminately, there''s ample evidence to show that they do shoot people discriminately, and are rarely punished for the resulting homicides, even when they involve the death of unarmed suspects or innocent bystanderd', '2004-12-01 01:20:38.000000', NULL, 0),
