(1042012, 122219, 19408, '<td valign="top">Personally, I agree the sun has authority over us but the image should illustrate the meaning. Air has authority over us, we all need it to live, but if you point the camera at nothing and submit a blurred blank picture is it going to go over well? You might title it "Air" and get some points. But that would be cleverly foolish.<br/> <br/>The image would have significance, for example, if there was a person waking up stretching his arms as the sun was rising. Meaning is indecipherable without such visual cues.<br/> <br/>It''s a nice picture just undevelopped.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-12-17 21:19:49.</i></td>', 'Personally, I agree the sun has authority over us but the image should illustrate the meaning. Air has authority over us, we all need it to live, but if you point the camera at nothing and submit a blurred blank picture is it going to go over well? You might title it "Air" and get some points. But that would be cleverly foolish. The image would have significance, for example, if there was a person waking up stretching his arms as the sun was rising. Meaning is indecipherable without such visual cues. It''s a nice picture just undevelopped.', '2004-12-01 19:13:57.000000', '2004-12-17 21:19:49.000000', 0),
(1042023, 123507, 20774, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for the comments. About the hat it''s what we get here in Portugal. But i guess i passed the message. Thanks again for every comment. Finally i seem to managed to make a photo that some people like. I thought i had the ribbon on my hands but it slipped right off, Better luck next time i hope. :) thanks once more seems like it''s never enough. ;)<br/> <br/>Seems that i got to emend this. I''m soooo happy with this ribbon. just makes me wanna do more photgraphy. i think one of my objectives is done. :)<br/> <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-12-02 15:11:55.</i></td>', 'Thanks everyone for the comments. About the hat it''s what we get here in Portugal. But i guess i passed the message. Thanks again for every comment. Finally i seem to managed to make a photo that some people like. I thought i had the ribbon on my hands but it slipped right off, Better luck next time i hope. :) thanks once more seems like it''s never enough. ;) Seems that i got to emend this. I''m soooo happy with this ribbon. just makes me wanna do more photgraphy. i think one of my objectives is done. :) ', '2004-12-01 19:23:06.000000', '2004-12-02 15:11:55.000000', 0),
(1042526, 123490, 3724, '<td valign="top">fyi a 6......  noted this foto during voting, I suspected that it was Native American subject, (now confirmed)having taught Jr High at Cheyenne River Res in Eagle Butte, SD, - a important experience for me.   The collaboration of students and teacher on this image makes sense as a learning experience but the result also gives a character to the image that is an unusual gift to this challenge and site. I am most happy that a connection has been made, especially with a picture that contains such honest expression of the idea, both in the title and in the powerful image.  My initial impression of the picture was that its only detriment was size.  Use of the full 640 pixal size tends to be important in a format and matrix that is small to begin with.  As for the editing, composition, colour etc. I can only say that the learning process goes on and on, both in making images and in looking at them.  For me this is very good work, with some impressive thought behind it.</td>', 'fyi a 6......  noted this foto during voting, I suspected that it was Native American subject, (now confirmed)having taught Jr High at Cheyenne River Res in Eagle Butte, SD, - a important experience for me.   The collaboration of students and teacher on this image makes sense as a learning experience but the result also gives a character to the image that is an unusual gift to this challenge and site. I am most happy that a connection has been made, especially with a picture that contains such honest expression of the idea, both in the title and in the powerful image.  My initial impression of the picture was that its only detriment was size.  Use of the full 640 pixal size tends to be important in a format and matrix that is small to begin with.  As for the editing, composition, colour etc. I can only say that the learning process goes on and on, both in making images and in looking at them.  For me this is very good work, with some impressive thought behind it.', '2004-12-01 23:17:04.000000', NULL, 0),
