(1132253, 123446, 656, '<td valign="top">Imaginative use of light - good idea and well executed.  I''d maybe like to see it shot from the ''other side'' looking more in to his face, with the shadow hanging over him, but a good interpretiation of the theme.</td>', 'Imaginative use of light - good idea and well executed.  I''d maybe like to see it shot from the ''other side'' looking more in to his face, with the shadow hanging over him, but a good interpretiation of the theme.', '2005-01-26 00:21:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1481802, 123538, 16488, '<td valign="top">When I saw you post this in the closest to 5 thread, I just assumed that it was for the "road sign" challenge.  So much for assumptions!  (I skipped "authority" as I had no clue or guts to enter.)<br/> <br/>It''s a funny pic and a funny title.  The quibbles could be qualmed with some different post-processing (though those may not have been available to you during the challenge).  I like photos of signs.  I think they''re very collectible.  Though they are often static subjects, your interesting background with its textures and the sky with simple clouds transcends the usual humdrum.<br/> <br/>(thanks for playing)</td>', 'When I saw you post this in the closest to 5 thread, I just assumed that it was for the "road sign" challenge.  So much for assumptions!  (I skipped "authority" as I had no clue or guts to enter.) It''s a funny pic and a funny title.  The quibbles could be qualmed with some different post-processing (though those may not have been available to you during the challenge).  I like photos of signs.  I think they''re very collectible.  Though they are often static subjects, your interesting background with its textures and the sky with simple clouds transcends the usual humdrum. (thanks for playing)', '2005-06-24 18:29:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1518904, 123523, 24454, '<td valign="top">I think the problem with this may be just one of those "dpc no-no''s" in that statutes and toys nearly always get dismissed.   Also, it may be a little "unsimple" in that the distractions of the shape of the figurine itself, then the red and the black where you can''t really tell what it is are pretty distracting.   I''m not sure I know what I''m talking about on all that, it''s just something that my "eye" tells me.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I think the problem with this may be just one of those "dpc no-no''s" in that statutes and toys nearly always get dismissed.   Also, it may be a little "unsimple" in that the distractions of the shape of the figurine itself, then the red and the black where you can''t really tell what it is are pretty distracting.   I''m not sure I know what I''m talking about on all that, it''s just something that my "eye" tells me. ', '2005-07-08 14:31:04.000000', NULL, 0),
